// An `@name` in decorator position that resolves to nothing is E0061 — reported by the CHECKER,
// not the parser. That distinction is the point: the directive name-space includes the installed
// extensions' directives, which the parser has no dependency on, so only the checker can tell a
// typo from a name an extension declares. The parser records the directive verbatim and resolves
// nothing.
//
// Its argument is not a syntax error either: the directive grammar was unified with `#[...]`'s,
// so `@openapi("petstore.yaml")` parses as a directive with one string argument. An extension that
// declares `openapi` makes this exact program legal with no front-end change.
// expect: error E0061 at 12:2
// expect: exit 1
@openapi("petstore.yaml")
struct Pet { name: string }
echo "unreached"
